=== corrections addressed (main review VD01-VD05 + current-gate status) ===
[VD01] verify_pins hashed bytes, but public JSON loaders reopened and parsed unchecked bytes; a replacement between pin pass and parse was consumed while the report still claimed the original verified digest.
fix: Every public document loader (load_json_document) reads the file once into an immutable byte buffer, verifies sha256 of that exact buffer against the context expected pin, then decodes the same buffer; missing/unreadable/changed inputs produce explicit blocked/failed outcomes and no unverified JSON is consumed. Helper imports hash and compile the same buffer.
regressions: SyntheticOfflineTests.test_replacement_between_pin_pass_and_parse_is_detected

[VD02] A missing pin masked an observed hash mismatch (corrupt-available + missing reported blocked 2 instead of failed 1); only one of the two lists was reported.
fix: Precedence: any observed corrupt/unreadable/invalid available input must be failed (exit 1); only all-missing prerequisites are blocked (exit 2). Mixed situations report both the missing list and the mismatch details. Explicit --scope force-offline without --archive is a missing prerequisite (blocked 2), while malformed CLI arguments remain usage_error.
regressions: SyntheticOfflineTests.test_missing_pin_does_not_mask_observed_corruption, RealPinnedDataTests.test_force_offline_without_archive_is_blocked_not_usage_error, RealPinnedDataTests.test_real_cli_usage_errors_are_deterministic

[VD03] VerificationSpec stored caller-owned mutable dicts, and any spec with name production was accepted (dataclasses.replace on a synthetic spec produced a production-labelled PASS over a 1056-byte synthetic archive).
fix: All spec containers are immutable copies on ingress (MappingProxyType over dict copies; tuples for sequences), so later caller mutations cannot alter the spec and direct spec-map writes fail. A production-labelled context must exactly match the immutable canonical PRODUCTION_SPEC fields/pins/counts/provenance before any data/helper read, otherwise it is rejected early with deterministic failed exit 1 and no helper execution. Custom contexts are explicitly reported as synthetic_fixture with production_provenance=false; there is no caller-supplied trusted flag.
regressions: SyntheticOfflineTests.test_spec_containers_are_immutable_ingress_copies, SyntheticOfflineTests.test_production_relabelled_spec_is_rejected_without_any_read

[VD04] --output could overwrite a pinned input (main reproduced with --output clone/data/preprocessing.json inside a cloned tree returning exit 0) while the report presented its prior bytes as verified.
fix: Before any output probe or write, the resolved/canonicalized output path is compared with all actually-read inputs (the 9 pinned paths, the selected archive, the verifier entrypoint), including equal-path spellings such as .. components and existing-file samefile aliases (hardlink/symlink/junction); a protected target is rejected with failed exit 1 and originals stay byte-identical. Legitimate report paths such as data/manifest.json remain allowed.
regressions: CliOutputProtectionTests.test_output_rejects_pinned_input_and_parent_alias, CliOutputProtectionTests.test_output_rejects_verifier_entrypoint, CliOutputProtectionTests.test_output_rejects_hardlink_alias_of_pinned_input, CliOutputProtectionTests.test_output_allows_legitimate_report_path

[VD05] The published unit suite required the private controller file verify-data-main-decisions.json and assumed a fixed worktree depth, so an ordinary peer checkout failed FileNotFoundError.
fix: The constants test compares pinned identity against literal expected 9 hashes/counts/contract written in the test file itself (from main decisions); no private controller file or .local tree is referenced. Real-archive integration cases are gated by the DEEPEYE_FORCE_ARCHIVE environment path and skip with a counted reason when unset (SkipContractTests enforces exactly 3 gated skips). The CLI default full scope no longer invents a 4-parent archive location: without an explicit --archive it reports archive status no_path (blocked 2) truthfully.
regressions: RealPinnedDataTests.test_production_constants_match_main_decisions, SkipContractTests.test_env_gated_skip_contract

[CURRENT-GATE] Stale missing-gate listing still included the causal curve input main acceptance even though CURVE05 pure builder acceptance is published.
fix: Removed the stale gate from missing_full_gates (CURVE05 pure builder accepted/published; curve-repair1-main-review.json, PR25 head fe9fc080). Four gates remain unresolved and the default full scope stays blocked with every product card not_run.
regressions: status-only (no runtime path change)

