- Main review VD01-VD05 reproduced the five defects above against the original five files; all five are corrected in this round with the regression tests listed under corrections_addressed (the original five files are preserved read-only in the director snapshot verify-data-before-main-review and in the local temp copy base5).
- Iteration incident (temp-only): an early directory probe used the mistyped path ...competition\depeye (6 chars) instead of deepeye (7 chars) and reported LOSS (exit 9) three times until corrected; all later helpers assert basename == deepeye and len == 7 (lottery_log.txt records LOSS x3 then WIN with 61 files).
- Iteration incident (temp-only): in-session patch application through the primary path was unreliable under this PowerShell session, so patches were applied via codex.exe --codex-run-as-apply-patch against a staging mirror with path-prefix rewriting (apply_patch_stage.py). The staged sources were then deployed to the product with before/after hash assertions (deploy_test.py).
- Iteration incident (owned file): an intermediate test-file revision (57333 bytes, sha256 1733e15006c24e37d57c449d9d1af77de590eeacd374b197cf01e62f07a37bf2) was present in the product test path during iteration (base + tp1 patch, re-applied deterministically in the temp reconstruction below). It was backed up to the temp dir and replaced by the final staged revision (71054 bytes, sha256 4fe3b827a4c5c6ccca65c3fb8e21099f70c96e42e6ebd19c0087b6b8a1974d74) with deploy assertions before any final run.
- Iteration incident (test-side only): three self-inflicted test-logic errors were found and fixed while iterating the stage suite. (1) The skip-contract test counted occurrences of the skip-reason literal in its own source and the assertion string itself added an extra occurrence (off-by-one); fixed by splitting the literal (tp2i/tp2j). (2) The spec-immutability test asserted production counts after replace(group_counts=...) instead of the caller snapshot (train: 999); corrected to the snapshot semantics plus inequality with PRODUCTION_SPEC (tp2i). (3) The legitimate-output test originally required the real archive and exit 0; rewritten (tp2f) to run without the archive and expect the truthful blocked exit 2 while output_write stays passed, which is checkout-portable. No product-code defect was involved in these three.
- After the stage suite reached 48 tests OK (env archive set), the staged bytes were deployed to the product; the five final runs (product suite with env archive, offline manifest emission, default full scope, immutable scope verification, clean-checkout suite) were executed against the product tree and all hashes were re-verified afterwards as recorded above.

=== limits ===
- Software-only correction round: this is not C01 acceptance and no product/hardware card is claimed; product_card_C01=not_run and every formal card remains not_run.
- The archive was hashed as a raw byte stream only: 0 ZIP members opened, 0 LAS values parsed, 0 statistics re-fit; the zipfile-spy regressions enforce the zero-open/zero-parse property.
- Runtime future-label access and real/sim (sensor_live vs sim_em_v2) domain separation remain unknown_not_run, never reported as zero. Four gates remain unresolved: R03 public resource/profile/observation schema acceptance; sensor_live whole acquisition-run manifest; sim_em_v2 whole-scenario and derivative splits; runtime future-label/truth-access instrumentation.
- Provider/model/effort are not observable from inside this ordinary executor session; the assignment dispatch record (route deepseek, instance deepseek-c-15, job child-21d7bc6b0d79417487812570710ab15b) and the assignment-stated DeepSeek Flash/max are recorded, never inferred from the model catalog.
